course: dictionary
lesson: 15668
title: Threefold: three times, or three parts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Threefold is made from three and fold. It can mean three times as much or as many. «The number of plants in the garden grew threefold after the rain.» If there were 2 plants and now there are 6, that is threefold, because 2 times 3 is 6.
explain: Threefold can also mean having three parts. «The team made a threefold plan: find food, find water, then build shelter.» Each part is a separate step, so count the parts to check the meaning.
explain: A quick check is to ask, "Is it three times bigger, or does it have three parts?" Then swap in "three times as much" or "in three parts" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Threefold means three times as much or as many: a threefold increase.
fact: Threefold also means having three parts: a threefold plan.
fact: Threefold can be an adjective or an adverb.
fact: In maths, a threefold increase means multiplying by three.
fact: «A threefold rise in prices» means the price went up to three times what it was before.
exercise: «The baker made a threefold batch of buns for the fair.» What does threefold mean here? | Three parts only | Half as many | *Three times as many | Very small
exercise: «The school's plan had a threefold goal: learn, play and share.» What does threefold tell us? | Three times as much | Something very old | *Three parts | Two parts
exercise: Which of these shows a threefold increase? | A list of 2 becomes 4 | *A list of 2 becomes 6 if it grows three times over | A list of 2 becomes 6 | A list of 2 becomes 1
test: Mia has 4 apples, and then she gets three times as many. How many apples does she have now? | *12 | 43 | 7 | 8
test: Ravi says a threefold plan has how many parts? | Four | Thirty | Two | *Three
exam: Which sentence uses threefold to mean three times as much? | The hall was ancient | *The crop grew threefold after the rain | The bus was barely full | The team made a threefold plan
